{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01En6BaqPgGLmZBNmHkycvqS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — Learning When to Verify: RL-Trained Selective Self-Verification for Interactive Agents\n2\t\n3\t> Post-MVP 重写 (2026-05-17) | D054 framing pivot + Dream Review feedback (weak reject → 修正理论)\n4\t\n5\t## Core Insight\n6\t\n7\tMulti-turn interactive agents 的 self-verification 大部分是 confirmatory（不改变行为）而非 corrective。训练 agent 学 selective verification 的前提是 RL 训练本身能 work。我们发现 LLM agent 社区默认的 step-independent training 在长 horizon 任务中灾难性崩溃，根因是**双机制失效**：\n8\t\n9\t1. **Policy Information Loss**: 短窗口（h 步）的 policy 无法学习跨步策略（如 \"先探索 drawer 再去 countertop\"）\n10\t2. **Advantage Sign Misattribution**: step_independent 中，per-window advantage 的**符号**由 episode 成败决定，而非 window-local action quality：\n11\t   - 失败 episode 中的好 action → 获得负 advantage（被错误惩罚）\n12\t   - 成功 episode 中的差 action → 获得正 advantage（被错误强化）\n13\t   - 梯度方向（reinforce/suppress）反映 episode outcome 而非 local decision quality\n14\t   - 附加：γ^k magnitude decay 使早期 window 信号更弱（γ^24 ≈ 29%, where 24 = ⌈T/h⌉-1 windows），但方向错误比幅度衰减更致命\n15\t\n16\tEpisode-level training 同时解决两者：policy 看全历史（解决 1），整条 trajectory 作为一个 GRPO 样本，所有 tokens 共享同一 advantage — 虽然仍是 episode-level credit（非 per-token），但消除了 window 间的 sign misattribution，因为不再需要将 episode reward 分配到独立优化的子窗口（解决 2）。\n17\t\n18\t**技术澄清**：GRPO 算法本身是 bandit-style（advantage = (R-μ)/σ，无显式 γ），但 RAGEN 的 step_independent 实现在 `compute_step_discounted_returns()` 中引入 γ 计算每个 window 的 return（代码：`agent_trainer.py:271-340`）。γ^(T-t) decay 对 step_independent 模式是代码事实，不是类比。Episode-level 模式下无此问题：整条 trajectory 只有一个 return = episode_reward。\n19\t\n20\t## Story Arc\n21\t\n22\t**Dual contribution**: Training methodology diagnosis + Selective verification system\n23\t\n24\t叙事线：\n25\t1. Self-verification 对 interactive agents 有用，但 always-on 成本高\n26\t2. 训练 agent 学 WHEN to verify 需要 RL → 但 LLM agent 社区默认的 step-independent training 在多轮任务上灾难性崩溃（0% at step 10）\n27\t3. 我们诊断双机制根因（information loss + advantage sign misattribution），提出 episode-level GRPO 解决\n28\t4. 分析 \"为什么社区默认走向 step-independent\"（context window 限制 + token-level training 惯性 + framework design accident）\n29\t5. 在 episode-level 基础上，用 action-change 作为 verification informativeness 的 reward，训练 selective policy\n30\t6. 结果：near-always-on performance + 显著降低 verification cost\n31\t\n32\t**定位**：不 claim \"发明了 episode-level RL\"（trivial），而是 \"诊断了 LLM agent RL 训练中被忽视的 step-independent 隐性代价 + 系统分析崩溃机制 + 提出实用修复方案 + 在此基础上实现 selective verification\"\n33\t\n34\t## Target Venue\n35\t\n36\t待定（NeurIPS 2026 / EMNLP 2026 / ICLR 2026），取决于实验进度和最终效果。\n37\t\n38\t## Core Claims\n39\t\n40\t### Claim 1 (strength: strong): Step-independent GRPO catastrophically fails for multi-turn agents due to dual mechanism\n41\t- 所需证据：episode-level vs step-independent 对比（多 seed），h-sweep ablation（3 seeds each），mechanistic analysis（gradient signal measurement），GAE baseline comparison\n42\t- 当前证据状态：**ESTABLISHED** (exp029 step5 val=25% vs exp028c step10 val=0%)\n43\t- 机制：(1) policy information loss (h-step context insufficient), (2) advantage sign misattribution (gradient direction reflects episode outcome, not window-local action quality; additionally γ^k magnitude decay for early windows)\n44\t- 技术细节：GRPO 算法无固有 γ，但 RAGEN step_independent 的 `compute_step_discounted_returns()` 引入 γ-discounted per-window returns → advantage 符号由 episode 成败决定。代码验证：`agent_trainer.py:271-340` + `core_algos.py:194-246`\n45\t\n46\t### Claim 2 (strength: moderate): Action-change is an effective intrinsic reward for verification informativeness\n47\t- 所需证据：selective verification 训练收敛 + action-change vs random/confidence baselines\n48\t- 当前证据状态：**not yet established**，依赖 Phase B 实验\n49\t- 前提：episode-level 训练的 agent 需达到 ≥40% success 才有意义\n50\t\n51\t### Claim 3 (strength: moderate): Learned selective policy matches always-on performance at reduced verification cost\n52\t- 所需证据：B-IAVR verification ↓40%+ 且 success delta < 3pp vs always-on\n53\t- 当前证据状态：**not yet established**，依赖 Phase B + C\n54\t- 前提：Claim 1 的 agent 需足够强\n55\t\n56\t## Contingency Plan\n57\t\n58\t如果 episode-level 训练收敛后 success 仍 < 40%（不足以支撑 cost-efficiency story）：\n59\t- **Plan A**：paper 变为 diagnostic + analysis contribution — \"Why Step-Independent RL Fails for LLM Multi-Turn Agents: Dual Mechanism Analysis\" (需更深 ablation + GAE comparison + community practice survey)\n60\t- **Plan B**：加 Self-Guide reward 到 episode-level（从 binary→dense reward），推高 performance 后再做 selective verification\n61\t- 不考虑 downgrade venue\n62\t- **注意**：Dream review 已证明 Plan A 纯 methodology paper 需要比预期更深的分析才能通过审稿（\"诊断社区默认实践的隐性代价\" > \"episode-level RL works\"）\n63\t\n64\t## Reviewer Attack Surface + Defense\n65\t\n66\t| # | Concern | Severity | Defense |\n67\t|---|---------|----------|---------|\n68\t| 1 | \"Episode-level RL is obvious / well-known\" | HIGH | h-sweep (3 seeds) 展示 non-trivial cliff + 双机制理论 + \"为什么社区默认 step-independent\" 分析 |\n69\t| 2 | \"Theory 与 GRPO 不匹配\" | HIGH | 精确区分：GRPO 算法无 γ，但 step_independent 实现引入 γ-discounted returns（代码引用）→ per-window advantage logging 实证 + 伪代码 |\n70\t| 3 | \"缺 GAE/标准 RL baselines\" | HIGH | 加 GAE(λ=0.95) + GAE(λ=1,γ=1) baseline，证明 episode-level GRPO 与 GAE 的差异 |\n71\t| 4 | \"Self-Guide 3x performance gap\" | HIGH | 正面回应：不同 paradigm (expert-guided vs from-scratch RL)，不同问题（Self-Guide 回避了训练问题） |\n72\t| 5 | Single environment (ALFWorld) | MEDIUM | ScienceWorld transfer (if resources permit) |\n73\t| 6 | Small model (1.7B) | MEDIUM | 定位 resource-constrained; 7B 验证 (conditional) |\n74\t| 7 | Action-change = noise vs signal | MEDIUM | Entropy-controlled analysis + causal intervention (Phase B) |\n75\t| 8 | 与 ARES 差异化不足 | LOW | Head-to-head 对比 + 方法论差异表 |\n76\t| 9 | \"Turn-PPO 已解决相同问题\" | HIGH | 精确区分：Turn-PPO 发现 uniform advantage (subset)，我们发现 sign misattribution (superset + 量化 γ^24≈29%)；解法相反 (finer vs coarser) |\n77\t\n78\t## Evidence Status Matrix\n79\t\n80\t| Claim | MVP Evidence | Research Evidence Needed | Priority |\n81\t|-------|-------------|--------------------------|----------|\n82\t| Claim 1 | exp029 vs exp028c (25% vs 0%) | h-value ablation, multi-seed, mechanism paper figure | P0 |\n83\t| Claim 2 | N/A | Phase B full implementation | P1 |\n84\t| Claim 3 | N/A | Phase B + C comparison suite | P1 |\n85\t\n86\t## Competitive Positioning\n87\t\n88\t| System | Method | Benchmark | Key Difference from Us |\n89\t|--------|--------|-----------|----------------------|\n90\t| Self-Guide (2026) | Always-on verification | ALFWorld 72.7% (1.7B) | We add selectivity via RL |\n91\t| ARES (2603.07915) | SFT router, continuous effort | 52.7% token reduction | SFT vs RL, continuous vs binary |\n92\t| Thinkless (NeurIPS'25) | RL control token | reasoning domain | Same RL philosophy, different domain |\n93\t| ReflAct (EMNLP'25) | Prompting GPT-4 | ALFWorld 93.3% | Different scale/approach |\n94\t| RAGEN (2025) | GRPO for agents | varies | Step-independent default, our baseline |\n95\t| **Turn-PPO (2512.17008)** | Turn-level MDP + value fn | reasoning tasks | \"Uniform advantage\" vs our \"sign misattribution\"; finer credit vs coarser |\n96\t| **GAGPO (2605.13217)** | Grouped value proxy, step-aligned | ALFWorld 93.5% (1.5B) | Finer-grained credit for performance; we diagnose mechanism failure |\n97\t| **MT-GRPO (2505.11821)** | Turn-level reward design | QA search tasks | Turn-level credit; we show coarser suffices |\n98\t| **iStar (ICLR'26)** | Implicit PRM + dual advantage | WebShop 86.5% | Learns step rewards; we show episode-level eliminates misattribution |\n99\t| **ArCHer (ICML'24)** | Hierarchical multi-turn RL | multi-turn agents | Foundational framework; establishes need for hierarchical structure |\n100\t| **HiPER (2602.16165)** | Hierarchical Plan-Execute RL | ALFWorld 97.4% (7B) | SOTA performance pursuit; we do mechanism diagnosis |\n101\t\n102\t### Positioning Strategy\n103\t\n104\t**核心差异化：Contrarian Solution。** 竞品（Turn-PPO, GAGPO, MT-GRPO, iStar, HiPER）一致认为 multi-turn RL 需要更细粒度的 credit assignment（turn-level, step-level, hierarchical），并用此提升性能。我们的贡献是诊断性的：\n105\t\n106\t1. **问题定义更精确**：Turn-PPO 发现 \"uniform advantage\" 问题（所有 turn 获得相同 advantage），我们发现更本质的 \"Advantage Sign Misattribution\"（advantage 符号由 episode outcome 决定而非 local action quality），并量化 γ^24 ≈ 29% 的 return 衰减。Sign misattribution 是 uniform advantage 的超集。\n107\t\n108\t2. **Contrarian solution**：所有竞品的解法都是引入更细的 credit（turn-level value, step-level PRM, hierarchical planner）。我们展示更粗的 episode-level credit 反而消除 sign misattribution，因为它避免了将 episode reward 错误分配到独立优化的子窗口。这挑战了 \"越细越好\" 的社区默认假设。\n109\t\n110\t3. **不同 contribution 维度**：GAGPO/HiPER 追求 ALFWorld 93-97% 的 SOTA performance（通过更好的 credit + 更复杂的架构）。我们不 compete on performance axis，而是回答 \"为什么社区默认的 step-independent 灾难性失败\" 这个诊断问题。两个 contribution 维度正交互补。\n111\t\n112\t4. **与 CA Survey 的关系**：Zhang (2604.09459) 系统化了 47 种 CA 方法，但未分析 CA 方法本身的 failure modes（何时更细粒度反而有害）。我们填补这一空白。\n113\t\n114\t## Research Phases\n115\t\n116\t1. **Phase A (DONE)**: Episode-level GRPO training — MVP passed, demonstrates Claim 1\n117\t2. **Phase A+**: Continue training to convergence (target ≥40% success), deploy tatsu parallel patch, multi-seed\n118\t3. **Phase B**: Implement selective verification with action-change reward — Claim 2 & 3\n119\t4. **Phase C**: Ablation suite — context window sweep, reward ablations, baseline comparisons\n120\t5. **Phase D**: (Conditional on resources) Multi-env / multi-model scaling\n121\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da28e4c8-513a-4f80-b06c-ad45442adc3b","uuid":"b968701f-5143-4911-a85c-529076bea145","timestamp":"2026-05-17T13:52:20.025Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_1/projects/cost-verify-agent-rl/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260517T133129/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — Learning When to Verify: RL-Trained Selective Self-Verification for Interactive Agents\n\n> Post-MVP 重写 (2026-05-17) | D054 framing pivot + Dream Review feedback (weak reject → 修正理论)\n\n## Core Insight\n\nMulti-turn interactive agents 的 self-verification 大部分是 confirmatory（不改变行为）而非 corrective。训练 agent 学 selective verification 的前提是 RL 训练本身能 work。我们发现 LLM agent 社区默认的 step-independent training 在长 horizon 任务中灾难性崩溃，根因是**双机制失效**：\n\n1. **Policy Information Loss**: 短窗口（h 步）的 policy 无法学习跨步策略（如 \"先探索 drawer 再去 countertop\"）\n2. **Advantage Sign Misattribution**: step_independent 中，per-window advantage 的**符号**由 episode 成败决定，而非 window-local action quality：\n   - 失败 episode 中的好 action → 获得负 advantage（被错误惩罚）\n   - 成功 episode 中的差 action → 获得正 advantage（被错误强化）\n   - 梯度方向（reinforce/suppress）反映 episode outcome 而非 local decision quality\n   - 附加：γ^k magnitude decay 使早期 window 信号更弱（γ^24 ≈ 29%, where 24 = ⌈T/h⌉-1 windows），但方向错误比幅度衰减更致命\n\nEpisode-level training 同时解决两者：policy 看全历史（解决 1），整条 trajectory 作为一个 GRPO 样本，所有 tokens 共享同一 advantage — 虽然仍是 episode-level credit（非 per-token），但消除了 window 间的 sign misattribution，因为不再需要将 episode reward 分配到独立优化的子窗口（解决 2）。\n\n**技术澄清**：GRPO 算法本身是 bandit-style（advantage = (R-μ)/σ，无显式 γ），但 RAGEN 的 step_independent 实现在 `compute_step_discounted_returns()` 中引入 γ 计算每个 window 的 return（代码：`agent_trainer.py:271-340`）。γ^(T-t) decay 对 step_independent 模式是代码事实，不是类比。Episode-level 模式下无此问题：整条 trajectory 只有一个 return = episode_reward。\n\n## Story Arc\n\n**Dual contribution**: Training methodology diagnosis + Selective verification system\n\n叙事线：\n1. Self-verification 对 interactive agents 有用，但 always-on 成本高\n2. 训练 agent 学 WHEN to verify 需要 RL → 但 LLM agent 社区默认的 step-independent training 在多轮任务上灾难性崩溃（0% at step 10）\n3. 我们诊断双机制根因（information loss + advantage sign misattribution），提出 episode-level GRPO 解决\n4. 分析 \"为什么社区默认走向 step-independent\"（context window 限制 + token-level training 惯性 + framework design accident）\n5. 在 episode-level 基础上，用 action-change 作为 verification informativeness 的 reward，训练 selective policy\n6. 结果：near-always-on performance + 显著降低 verification cost\n\n**定位**：不 claim \"发明了 episode-level RL\"（trivial），而是 \"诊断了 LLM agent RL 训练中被忽视的 step-independent 隐性代价 + 系统分析崩溃机制 + 提出实用修复方案 + 在此基础上实现 selective verification\"\n\n## Target Venue\n\n待定（NeurIPS 2026 / EMNLP 2026 / ICLR 2026），取决于实验进度和最终效果。\n\n## Core Claims\n\n### Claim 1 (strength: strong): Step-independent GRPO catastrophically fails for multi-turn agents due to dual mechanism\n- 所需证据：episode-level vs step-independent 对比（多 seed），h-sweep ablation（3 seeds each），mechanistic analysis（gradient signal measurement），GAE baseline comparison\n- 当前证据状态：**ESTABLISHED** (exp029 step5 val=25% vs exp028c step10 val=0%)\n- 机制：(1) policy information loss (h-step context insufficient), (2) advantage sign misattribution (gradient direction reflects episode outcome, not window-local action quality; additionally γ^k magnitude decay for early windows)\n- 技术细节：GRPO 算法无固有 γ，但 RAGEN step_independent 的 `compute_step_discounted_returns()` 引入 γ-discounted per-window returns → advantage 符号由 episode 成败决定。代码验证：`agent_trainer.py:271-340` + `core_algos.py:194-246`\n\n### Claim 2 (strength: moderate): Action-change is an effective intrinsic reward for verification informativeness\n- 所需证据：selective verification 训练收敛 + action-change vs random/confidence baselines\n- 当前证据状态：**not yet established**，依赖 Phase B 实验\n- 前提：episode-level 训练的 agent 需达到 ≥40% success 才有意义\n\n### Claim 3 (strength: moderate): Learned selective policy matches always-on performance at reduced verification cost\n- 所需证据：B-IAVR verification ↓40%+ 且 success delta < 3pp vs always-on\n- 当前证据状态：**not yet established**，依赖 Phase B + C\n- 前提：Claim 1 的 agent 需足够强\n\n## Contingency Plan\n\n如果 episode-level 训练收敛后 success 仍 < 40%（不足以支撑 cost-efficiency story）：\n- **Plan A**：paper 变为 diagnostic + analysis contribution — \"Why Step-Independent RL Fails for LLM Multi-Turn Agents: Dual Mechanism Analysis\" (需更深 ablation + GAE comparison + community practice survey)\n- **Plan B**：加 Self-Guide reward 到 episode-level（从 binary→dense reward），推高 performance 后再做 selective verification\n- 不考虑 downgrade venue\n- **注意**：Dream review 已证明 Plan A 纯 methodology paper 需要比预期更深的分析才能通过审稿（\"诊断社区默认实践的隐性代价\" > \"episode-level RL works\"）\n\n## Reviewer Attack Surface + Defense\n\n| # | Concern | Severity | Defense |\n|---|---------|----------|---------|\n| 1 | \"Episode-level RL is obvious / well-known\" | HIGH | h-sweep (3 seeds) 展示 non-trivial cliff + 双机制理论 + \"为什么社区默认 step-independent\" 分析 |\n| 2 | \"Theory 与 GRPO 不匹配\" | HIGH | 精确区分：GRPO 算法无 γ，但 step_independent 实现引入 γ-discounted returns（代码引用）→ per-window advantage logging 实证 + 伪代码 |\n| 3 | \"缺 GAE/标准 RL baselines\" | HIGH | 加 GAE(λ=0.95) + GAE(λ=1,γ=1) baseline，证明 episode-level GRPO 与 GAE 的差异 |\n| 4 | \"Self-Guide 3x performance gap\" | HIGH | 正面回应：不同 paradigm (expert-guided vs from-scratch RL)，不同问题（Self-Guide 回避了训练问题） |\n| 5 | Single environment (ALFWorld) | MEDIUM | ScienceWorld transfer (if resources permit) |\n| 6 | Small model (1.7B) | MEDIUM | 定位 resource-constrained; 7B 验证 (conditional) |\n| 7 | Action-change = noise vs signal | MEDIUM | Entropy-controlled analysis + causal intervention (Phase B) |\n| 8 | 与 ARES 差异化不足 | LOW | Head-to-head 对比 + 方法论差异表 |\n| 9 | \"Turn-PPO 已解决相同问题\" | HIGH | 精确区分：Turn-PPO 发现 uniform advantage (subset)，我们发现 sign misattribution (superset + 量化 γ^24≈29%)；解法相反 (finer vs coarser) |\n\n## Evidence Status Matrix\n\n| Claim | MVP Evidence | Research Evidence Needed | Priority |\n|-------|-------------|--------------------------|----------|\n| Claim 1 | exp029 vs exp028c (25% vs 0%) | h-value ablation, multi-seed, mechanism paper figure | P0 |\n| Claim 2 | N/A | Phase B full implementation | P1 |\n| Claim 3 | N/A | Phase B + C comparison suite | P1 |\n\n## Competitive Positioning\n\n| System | Method | Benchmark | Key Difference from Us |\n|--------|--------|-----------|----------------------|\n| Self-Guide (2026) | Always-on verification | ALFWorld 72.7% (1.7B) | We add selectivity via RL |\n| ARES (2603.07915) | SFT router, continuous effort | 52.7% token reduction | SFT vs RL, continuous vs binary |\n| Thinkless (NeurIPS'25) | RL control token | reasoning domain | Same RL philosophy, different domain |\n| ReflAct (EMNLP'25) | Prompting GPT-4 | ALFWorld 93.3% | Different scale/approach |\n| RAGEN (2025) | GRPO for agents | varies | Step-independent default, our baseline |\n| **Turn-PPO (2512.17008)** | Turn-level MDP + value fn | reasoning tasks | \"Uniform advantage\" vs our \"sign misattribution\"; finer credit vs coarser |\n| **GAGPO (2605.13217)** | Grouped value proxy, step-aligned | ALFWorld 93.5% (1.5B) | Finer-grained credit for performance; we diagnose mechanism failure |\n| **MT-GRPO (2505.11821)** | Turn-level reward design | QA search tasks | Turn-level credit; we show coarser suffices |\n| **iStar (ICLR'26)** | Implicit PRM + dual advantage | WebShop 86.5% | Learns step rewards; we show episode-level eliminates misattribution |\n| **ArCHer (ICML'24)** | Hierarchical multi-turn RL | multi-turn agents | Foundational framework; establishes need for hierarchical structure |\n| **HiPER (2602.16165)** | Hierarchical Plan-Execute RL | ALFWorld 97.4% (7B) | SOTA performance pursuit; we do mechanism diagnosis |\n\n### Positioning Strategy\n\n**核心差异化：Contrarian Solution。** 竞品（Turn-PPO, GAGPO, MT-GRPO, iStar, HiPER）一致认为 multi-turn RL 需要更细粒度的 credit assignment（turn-level, step-level, hierarchical），并用此提升性能。我们的贡献是诊断性的：\n\n1. **问题定义更精确**：Turn-PPO 发现 \"uniform advantage\" 问题（所有 turn 获得相同 advantage），我们发现更本质的 \"Advantage Sign Misattribution\"（advantage 符号由 episode outcome 决定而非 local action quality），并量化 γ^24 ≈ 29% 的 return 衰减。Sign misattribution 是 uniform advantage 的超集。\n\n2. **Contrarian solution**：所有竞品的解法都是引入更细的 credit（turn-level value, step-level PRM, hierarchical planner）。我们展示更粗的 episode-level credit 反而消除 sign misattribution，因为它避免了将 episode reward 错误分配到独立优化的子窗口。这挑战了 \"越细越好\" 的社区默认假设。\n\n3. **不同 contribution 维度**：GAGPO/HiPER 追求 ALFWorld 93-97% 的 SOTA performance（通过更好的 credit + 更复杂的架构）。我们不 compete on performance axis，而是回答 \"为什么社区默认的 step-independent 灾难性失败\" 这个诊断问题。两个 contribution 维度正交互补。\n\n4. **与 CA Survey 的关系**：Zhang (2604.09459) 系统化了 47 种 CA 方法，但未分析 CA 方法本身的 failure modes（何时更细粒度反而有害）。我们填补这一空白。\n\n## Research Phases\n\n1. **Phase A (DONE)**: Episode-level GRPO training — MVP passed, demonstrates Claim 1\n2. **Phase A+**: Continue training to convergence (target ≥40% success), deploy tatsu parallel patch, multi-seed\n3. **Phase B**: Implement selective verification with action-change reward — Claim 2 & 3\n4. **Phase C**: Ablation suite — context window sweep, reward ablations, baseline comparisons\n5. **Phase D**: (Conditional on resources) Multi-env / multi-model scaling\n","numLines":121,"startLine":1,"totalLines":121}}}
